& [PurposeAndMeaning]
  + [LTO-001] compile one exact supplied term-candidate pool into the unique best feasible bounded term set under one declared context policy and total objective ordering without generating terms invoking a model or mutating a stitch
  + [LTO-002] optimal means only relative to the exact supplied pool coverage graph model profile task class horizon scope budgets threshold metrics and tie break; global semantic optimality and inference acceleration are not claimed

& [ProfilesAndBounds]
  + [LTO-003] request profile is cantor-sjs-lookahead-term-set-request/0.1 envelope profile is cantor-sjs-lookahead-term-set-envelope/0.1 verification profile is cantor-sjs-lookahead-term-set-verification/0.1 and evidence profile is cantor-sjs-lookahead-term-set-evidence/0.1
  + [LTO-004] strict compact UTF-8 canonical JSON refuses unknown duplicate noncanonical and trailing content and is bounded to request bytes 1048576 evidence bytes 8388608 depth 40 fields 16384 and ordinary text 4096
  + [LTO-005] candidates are 1 through 16 obligations 1 through 64 coverage edges 1 through 256 selected candidates 1 through 8 projected bytes at most 8192 token estimate at most 4096 and every integer operation is checked
  + [LTO-006] input class is exactly synthetic_provider_free_fixture or supplied_unobserved_candidate_pool and the retained fixture cannot be relabeled as supplied unobserved

& [ScopeObligationsAndCandidates]
  + [LTO-007] request binds distinct nonnil lowercase UUID-bearing request run scope policy and receipt identities exact source snapshots input class nonauthority evidence references and self-excluding request digest
  + [LTO-008] SelectionScope binds subject objective phase feature requirement artifact task class exact model profile horizon context assembly tool policy authority ceiling compiled-stitch profile and scope digest
  + [LTO-009] Obligation kind is exactly governing_requirement current_decision action_coordinate evidence_gate or known_fault; each obligation binds identity supplied weight 1 through 10000 mandatory flag source identity and exact scope
  + [LTO-010] every mandatory governing requirement denial and nonauthority boundary must be represented as a governing_requirement obligation and mandatory obligations can be covered only by governing_anchor candidates
  + [LTO-011] TermCandidate binds identity semantic identity subject anchor semantic turn transform scope source binding completion cue invalidators placement role dependency rank projected surface UTF-8 bytes token estimate and self-excluding digest
  + [LTO-012] source class is exactly governing_anchor plan_hint observed_coordinate or nonauthority_evidence; only governing_anchor may carry imported authority and selection never promotes another class
  + [LTO-013] candidate metric account supplies integers 0 through 10000 for decision relevance ambiguity reduction action relevance evidence relevance fault avoidance anchoring risk unsupported inference risk and stale distance; P0 does not infer or calibrate them
  + [LTO-014] CoverageEdge binds one candidate one obligation and one exact supplied relation identity; unknown cross-scope duplicate or governing-coverage-by-nonauthority edges fail closed

& [FeasibilityAndOptimization]
  + [LTO-015] SelectionPolicy binds maximum selected count projected-byte and token budgets required weighted-coverage basis points 1 through 10000 metric precedence source precedence placement precedence and policy digest
  + [LTO-016] normalization applies only to declared sets: identities coverage edges evidence references and invalidators sort uniquely while semantic strings and projected surface remain byte exact
  + [LTO-017] every nonempty subset through the selection ceiling is enumerated in increasing cardinality from the complete admitted candidate pool; at most sixteen candidates and eight selected bound the search
  + [LTO-018] one subset is feasible only when it covers every mandatory obligation stays within count byte and token budgets and floor covered-weight times 10000 divided by total-weight meets the required coverage basis points
  + [LTO-019] checked arithmetic computes covered weight coverage basis points bytes tokens and metric totals; overflow division-by-zero or impossible bound emits typed refusal and no partial envelope
  + [LTO-020] feasible subsets are totally ordered by smallest selected count then highest weighted coverage then highest decision ambiguity action evidence and fault-avoidance totals then lowest anchoring unsupported stale bytes and tokens then lexicographically smallest candidate identity vector
  + [LTO-021] exhaustive enumeration and the total ordering prove the selected set is uniquely optimal only under this exact objective; a heuristic score approximate search probabilistic tie or early exit is forbidden
  + [LTO-022] domination is reported when one same-scope candidate covers a superset with no worse cost risk staleness and no lower positive metrics with at least one strict improvement; P0 still enumerates the complete pool so domination cannot erase a feasible witness
  + [LTO-023] selected projection order is source precedence then dependency rank then placement precedence then candidate identity and is independent of enumeration or score order

& [AccountsAndFailure]
  + [LTO-024] result status is exactly selected_exact insufficient_budget or uncoverable_mandatory; insufficient and uncoverable outcomes retain every uncovered obligation and best partial witness but authorize no term set
  + [LTO-025] CandidateAccount disposition is exactly selected dominated feasible_not_selected or ineligible and records coverage objective contribution cost risk reason and comparator when applicable
  + [LTO-026] OptimizationReceipt binds admitted subset count feasible subset count selected identities rejected accounts uncovered accounts budget account objective tuple request and envelope digests and self-excluding receipt digest
  + [LTO-027] equal inputs produce byte-identical envelope receipt verification and evidence; unknown duplicate stale digest source promotion edge scope budget threshold metric tie account objective raw-byte and fully redigested semantic tampering fail closed
  + [LTO-028] independent verification reparses retained request bytes recomputes twice enumerates all subsets byte-compares envelope accounts receipt verification and reconstructed evidence manifest without trusting producer scores counts or chosen identities

& [AuthorityAndFixture]
  + [LTO-029] production exposes supplied-data parsing normalization hashing bounded selection accounting and independent verification only and performs no filesystem environment clock process network provider model inference embedding prompt mutation stitch mutation MCP Git workspace secret permission activation remote hardware or external action
  + [LTO-030] first fixture is synthetic provider-free with eight candidates six obligations twelve coverage edges selection ceiling three ninety-two enumerated subsets three selected five rejected one dominated zero uncovered one unique optimum and fourteen zero effect counters
  + [LTO-031] P0 emits selected structured candidates compatible with later LookaheadStitch construction but does not construct activate project or host a stitch
  + [LTO-032] repository candidate extraction empirical weights tokenizer accuracy prompt placement live A B speed or quality claims adaptive learning autonomy durable custody successor activation remote machines FPGA Minecraft and every physical effect remain separately sourced and signed

& [Acceptance]
  + [LTO-A01] source audit constraints delineation data dual threat seven-fold canonical explosion justification solution plan matrix phase lock proof review signature manifest and independent formation verifier agree exactly
  + [LTO-A02] safe Rust exports strict bounded forms exact enumeration total ordering complete accounts receipts and independent verification using existing dependencies only
  + [LTO-A03] focused success permutation tie dominance mandatory uncovered budget source authority scope digest raw-byte fully-redigested tamper and bounded complexity tests plus two CLIs retained evidence pass debug and overflow-checked release
  + [LTO-A04] exact locked offline serialized workspace debug release warnings-denied Clippy format formation runtime recursive evidence attribution publication remote equality and post-push replay pass
  + [LTO-A05] no generated semantics global optimality tokenizer accuracy inference speed quality prompt model provider autonomy host hardware or effect claim is inferred

& [Invalidation]
  + source identity scope schema bound obligation candidate edge metric objective ordering account receipt verification evidence requirement support artifact binding attribution or publication drift
